infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Pre-aggregated metrics vs sampled traces
  desc RED + USE summarise every request; traces keep the full path but only for a sampled few — exemplars bridge the two
  compares
    - label Pre-aggregated metrics (RED + USE)
      children
        - label 100% coverage
          desc Every request and second counted — no observation thrown away
        - label Bounded storage
          desc ~3 KB RAM per series; cardinality is the planned budget
        - label Only bounded labels
          desc route, method, status_class, service, region
        - label Cannot hold trace_id
          desc Unbounded values would multiply series into the billions
    - label Sampled traces
      children
        - label 0.1–5% head sampled
          desc Drop most of the common path to control cost
        - label 100% tail on errors / slow
          desc Requests over the SLO target always keep a trace
        - label Holds high-cardinality data
          desc trace_id, user_id, request_id live here, not in labels
        - label Full span tree per trace
          desc Whole request path — too heavy to keep for every request
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b
